        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-27",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "┌─────────┐"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-28",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "│   DB    │"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-29",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "└─────────┘"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-30",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "```"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-31",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "You’d want the engine to choose which variant to render depending on terminal width (wide → horizontal flow; narrow → vertical stack)."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-32",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Would you like me to also show how edge routing (like orthogonal connectors avoiding overlaps) might appear in such a sketch?"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-33",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "---"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-34",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Short answer: add a **measure pass** before layout that (a) wraps text to the available width, (b) computes display width with `wcwidth` (grapheme-aware), and (c) adds padding + borders. Boxes then use `max(contentWidth) × lines` as their intrinsic size; layout can grow/shrink from there."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-35",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "What to implement"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-36",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "1. **Normalize text**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-37",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- Strip ANSI (for length calc), keep a parallel “styled” buffer for rendering."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-38",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- Split into lines; segment by grapheme clusters (emoji, ZWJ) not code units."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-39",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "2. **Display width**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-40",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- Use `wcwidth`style width per grapheme (handles East Asian widths & emoji)."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-41",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- `displayWidth(line) = Σ wcwidth(grapheme_i)`."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-42",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "3. **Wrapping policy**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-43",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- Given `wrapAt`, soft-wrap words without breaking graphemes."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-44",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- If `wrapAt` is unknown (auto), compute **intrinsic** width from longest line; clamp later by container."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-45",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "4. **Box size**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-46",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- `contentW = max(displayWidth(wrappedLines))`"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-47",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- `contentH = wrappedLines.length`"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-48",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- `w = contentW + paddingLeft + paddingRight + borderLeft + borderRight`"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-49",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- `h = contentH + paddingTop + paddingBottom + borderTop + borderBottom`"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-50",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- Respect `min/max` constraints; if width shrinks later, re-wrap and re-measure."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-51",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "5. **Two-pass layout**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-52",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- **Pass 1 (intrinsic):** measure each node with “infinite” width cap (or a heuristic cap like 60)."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-53",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- **Pass 2 (constrained):** flex/grid allocates widths; for nodes whose width changed, **re-wrap → re-measure**; iterate until stable or 2–3 passes."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-54",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "6. **Elision for ultra-narrow**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-55",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- If `wrapAt < 3`, elide to `…` or initials."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-56",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Minimal TS sketch (drop-in)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-57",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "```tsx"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-58",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "// Minimal helpers — provide real implementations in your engine:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-59",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "const stripAnsi = (s: string) => s.replace("
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-60",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "// ANSI SGR escapes"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-61",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "/\\x1B\\[[0-9;]*m/g, ''"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-62",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ");"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-63",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "const graphemes = (s: string) =>"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-64",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "// Prefer Intl.Segmenter if available; fallback naive split"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-65",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "(globalThis as any).Intl?.Segmenter"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-66",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "? Array.from(new (Intl as any).Segmenter('en', {granularity:'grapheme'}).segment(s), (x:any)=>x.segment)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-67",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ": Array.from(s);"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-68",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "// Placeholder; swap in a real wcwidth (east asian + emoji aware)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-69",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "function wcwidthGrapheme(g: string): number {"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-70",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "// crude: wide CJK/emoji = 2, control = 0, else 1"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-71",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "if (/[\\u{1F300}-\\u{1FAFF}\\u{1F900}-\\u{1F9FF}]/u.test(g)) return 2;"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-72",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "if (/[\\u1100-\\u115F\\u2E80-\\uA4CF\\uAC00-\\uD7A3\\uF900-\\uFAFF\\uFE10-\\uFE19\\uFE30-\\uFE6F\\uFF00-\\uFF60\\uFFE0-\\uFFE6]/.test(g)) return 2;"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-73",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "if (/[\\x00-\\x1F\\x7F]/.test(g)) return 0;"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-74",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "return 1;"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-75",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-76",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "function displayWidth(s: string): number {"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-77",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "return graphemes(stripAnsi(s)).reduce((w, g) => w + wcwidthGrapheme(g), 0);"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-78",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-79",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "function wrapLine(line: string, wrapAt: number): string[] {"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-80",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "if (wrapAt === Infinity) return [line];"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-81",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "const out: string[] = [];"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-82",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "let cur: string[] = [];"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-83",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "let curW = 0;"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-84",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "for (const g of graphemes(line)) {"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-85",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "const w = wcwidthGrapheme(g);"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-86",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "if (curW + w > wrapAt && cur.length) {"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-87",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "out.push(cur.join(''));"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-88",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "cur = [g];"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-89",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "curW = w;"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-90",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "} else {"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-91",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "cur.push(g); curW += w;"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-92",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-93",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-94",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "if (cur.length) out.push(cur.join(''));"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-95",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "return out;"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-96",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-97",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "type Padding = {t:number,r:number,b:number,l:number};"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-98",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "type Border = {t:number,r:number,b:number,l:number}; // 0 or 1 per side"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-99",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "type MeasureOpts = {"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-100",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "wrapAt?: number; // content width cap (excludes padding/borders)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-101",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "padding?: Padding;"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-102",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "border?: Border;"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-103",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "minW?: number; maxW?: number; minH?: number; maxH?: number;"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-104",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "};"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-105",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "export function measureBox(text: string|string[], opts: MeasureOpts = {}) {"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-106",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "const lines = Array.isArray(text) ? text : text.split('\\n');"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-107",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "const pad = {t:0,r:1,b:0,l:1, ...(opts.padding||{})};"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-108",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "const bor = {t:1,r:1,b:1,l:1, ...(opts.border||{})};"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-109",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "// First pass: intrinsic (no wrap cap) to get a reasonable starting width"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-110",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "const intrinsicLines = lines.flatMap(l => wrapLine(l, opts.wrapAt ?? Infinity));"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-111",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "let contentW = Math.max(1, ...intrinsicLines.map(displayWidth));"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-112",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "let contentH = intrinsicLines.length;"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-113",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "// Apply min/max to content width, not total width"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-114",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "const minContentW = Math.max(0, (opts.minW ?? 0) - (pad.l+pad.r) - (bor.l+bor.r));"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-115",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "const maxContentW = (opts.maxW ?? Infinity) - (pad.l+pad.r) - (bor.l+bor.r);"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-116",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "const targetContentW = Math.min(Math.max(contentW, minContentW), maxContentW);"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-117",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "// If we must shrink, re-wrap to target width and recompute height"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-118",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "if (targetContentW < contentW) {"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-119",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "const wrapped = lines.flatMap(l => wrapLine(l, targetContentW));"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-120",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "contentW = Math.max(1, ...wrapped.map(displayWidth));"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-121",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "contentH = wrapped.length;"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-122",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-123",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "// Clamp height if needed (rare; usually unbounded)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-124",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "const minH = opts.minH ?? 0, maxH = opts.maxH ?? Infinity;"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-125",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "contentH = Math.min(Math.max(contentH, minH), maxH);"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-126",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "const totalW = contentW + pad.l + pad.r + bor.l + bor.r;"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-127",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "const totalH = contentH + pad.t + pad.b + bor.t + bor.b;"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-128",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "return {contentW, contentH, totalW, totalH};"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-129",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-130",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "```"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-131",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "How it fits the engine"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-136",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-132",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**Measure phase:** call `measureBox(node.content, {wrapAt, padding, border, min/max})` to get intrinsic size."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-133",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**Layout phase:** assign each node a `wrapAt` (content width cap) from the container/flex calculation."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-134",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**Stability loop:** if assigned width differs from measured width, re-wrap + re-measure, then finalize."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-135",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**Render:** pad each line to `contentW`, draw borders, then content."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-137",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Quick sanity checks"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-141",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-138",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "ASCII name (“Service API”) → width grows to fit; when terminal narrows, it wraps to two lines and height grows."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-139",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Emoji (“DB 🔒”) → counts as width 2; box widens accordingly."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-140",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "CJK (“服务网关”) → width 2 per char; box doubles correctly."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-142",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "If you want, I can wire this into a tiny demo that prints boxes with dynamic sizes and shows how they reflow at 120, 90, 60, 40 cols."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-143",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "---"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}